This is the file (obviously the one without .readme at the end) you have to put in your ~/.ssh folder to make sure you can do things like:
ssh pandia
and not worry about IP addresses and usernames depending on where are you connecting (CVMs vs. hosts), and such.
permissions should be 600: chmod 600 ~/.ssh/config

It assumes your public key is named id_rsa and is in ~/.ssh folder. This can be tweaked if you have it differently.
How to generate the public and private key pairs on Linux (no need to do any changes in sshd_config file!):
https://www.maketecheasier.com/generate-public-private-ssh-key/

